// P06 reusable semantic performance adapter (docs/the-better-one/P06_13S_PERFORMANCE_SYSTEM_IMPLEMENTATION_DIRECTIVE.md §1–§3).
// PURE and versioned. It consumes the APPROVED PerformanceCommand packet (schemas/performance_command_v1.schema.json, a byte copy of
// docs/the-better-one/PERFORMANCE_COMMAND_SCHEMA_V1.json) and compiles it into the EXISTING plan surfaces that temporal.mjs already executes:
//   aim layer          plan.__gaze[rig.joint][]            (look_at, turn_head rigid, point)        → temporal.mjs#evalPrimary
//   channel swaps      plan.__acting_events[]              (blink, speak, change_expression, react, grip/release/point hand states)
//                                                                                                  → state_channels.mjs#channelEvents
//   joint tracks       plan.tracks[rig].joints[j]          (react body beat, profile anticipation) → temporal.mjs#rawJoint
//   windowed additive  plan.__additive[rig.joint][]        (idle breathing inside its interval)     → temporal.mjs#addAt
//   contacts           doc.actions[].contact_events        (grip→release hold, turn_body plants)    → temporal.mjs#solveConstraints
//   reach ramps        plan.reaches / plan.grips           (reach approach, release retract)        → temporal.mjs#contactsAt, art_demand
//   view swaps         doc.actions[].view_events           (turn_head view cel, turn_body)          → state_router + state_timeline
//   gait cels          plan.cels[action]                   (walk on APPROVED_CELS)                  → temporal.mjs#celsAt
// There is no second clock or timeline: the same compiled plan drives Neutrino frames, art demand, QA and the production stages.
// Every refusal is a typed BridgeError whose details carry {action_id, command_id, owner, frame_range, failed_invariant, earliest_producer,
// needed_art_or_capability, user_approval_needed}. Nothing here knows a character name: roles come from the packet's reviewed role_map,
// limits/states/sockets from the measured rig, style values from the approved character performance profile.
